    "blurb": "The RFK performance delivers a soaring Morning Dew opener, a monster Dark Star → He's Gone sequence and a blistering Bird Song jam. Jerry’s tone is immaculate, Phil’s bass drives the extended improvisations, and Keith adds rich piano textures. Soundboard recordings capture every nuance of this high‑energy marathon.",
    "review": "June 10, 1973 at RFK Stadium finds the Dead in full marathon mode, launching the night with a shivering Morning Dew that instantly sets a lofty bar. The first set weaves through classics like Jack Straw and Box of Rain before the band dives into an expansive Bird Song that showcases Keith’s piano flourishes and Bill’s crisp drumming. Set two erupts with a flawless Eyes Of The World segueing into Stella Blue, then explodes on Dark Star → He's Gone, where Garcia’s improvisational fire meets Phil’s “bombs” bass, while the Allman Brothers guests add extra heat during the Wharf Rat/Truckin' stretch. The third set caps the evening with soulful vocal moments on It Takes A Lot To Laugh… and a rousing Not Fade Away jam that leaves the stadium buzzing. Across all available sources, Miller’s sound‑board transfer (gd1973-06-10.sbd.miller.fix-89640.89730.flac16) offers crystal‑clear balance, making it the definitive listening experience for this legendary show.",
